Add the following type constructor: A1sz

A1sz(T) is for an array of elements of type T where the size of the
array is attached.

We need to following operations on A1sz:

a1sz_size[T]: A1sz(T) -> sint

a1sz_getat[T]: (A1sz(T), sint) -> T
Given an array A and an index i, a1sz_getat returns A[i]

a1sz_setat[T]: (A1sz(T), sint, T) -> void
Given an array A and an index i and an element x, a1sz_setat updates A[i] with x

For creating arrays:

a1sz_make_ncpy[T]: (sint, T) -> A1sz(T)
Given an integer n (size) and an element x of type T,
a1sz_make_ncpy returns an array A of size n such that A[i] contains x for each valid index i

a1sz_make_nfun[T]: (sint, sint -> T) -> A1sz(T)
Given an integer n (size) and an function f from sint to T,
a1sz_make_nfun returns an array A of size n such that A[i] contains f(i) for each valid index i

Also add support for lazy-evaluation.

Add a type constructor Lazy(T) for a delayed computation returning a value of type T.
Here are some basic operations for Lazy:

lazy_eval[T]: lazy(T) -> T
lazy_make[T]: (() -> T) -> lazy(T)

Now add another constructor stcn, which can be defined as follows using ML-like syntax:

datatype
Stcn(T) =
| stcn_nil of ()
| stcn_cons of (T, Strm(T))
where Strm(T) = Lazy(Stcn(T))

We need the followng basic operations:

stcn_nilq[T]: stcn(T) -> bool
stcn_consq[T]: stcn(T) -> bool

stcn_head[T]: stcn(T) -> T
stcn_tail[T]: stcn(T) -> strm(T)

